\paragraph{Per-model detection baselines.}
ConStat achieves AUROC 0.73 on non-RL models (Table~\ref{tab:constat}) but degrades to 0.44 on RL models, consistent with PPO's smoothing of original-vs-reformulated accuracy gaps (effect size drops from 0.85 to 0.31). DVD detects verbatim contamination at AUROC 0.66 (Table~\ref{tab:dvd}) but is weak on variant contamination (0.58) and costly (65 GPU-hours for 12 models). These per-model approaches are complementary to DIF's group-level analysis.

