\paragraph{Practical recommendation.} Architecture stratification is simple, zero-cost, and immediately actionable: when applying DIF to LLM benchmarks, restrict the analysis to architecture-homogeneous subpopulations. This reduces spurious flags from architecture confounding while improving IRT model assumptions.


\subsection{Semi-Synthetic Validation Results}
\label{sec:semi_synthetic_results}

Table~\ref{tab:semi_synthetic} presents semi-synthetic validation results across benchmarks and matching strategies. On MMLU, cross-subject matching achieves $\Delta\text{TPR} = +0.508$ at injection probability $p = 0.5$, with strict $\Delta\text{FPR} = 0.000$ (4/5 subjects show $\Delta\text{TPR} > 0.3$). Within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination, inflating FPR by +0.186. The dose-response relationship (increasing $\Delta$TPR from $p = 0.3$ to $p = 1.0$) confirms the signal is driven by injected contamination rather than distributional artifacts.

Cross-benchmark replication on GSM8K (1{,}319 items $\times$ 6{,}702 models from METABENCH) yields $\Delta\text{TPR} = +0.818$ with standard matching and $+0.517$ with external matching, confirming framework portability. GSM8K's temporal DIF rate is C\% = 18.9\%, lower than MMLU's 31.3\%, consistent with its narrower construct (single-domain math).

